I did not add the two operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs filesystem access, and calling the metadata service needs `aap:caps/http-client`. Neither is granted, and a target of `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter has no file access anyway. Sending the input's text in a URL would also move untrusted data to an outside service. If operations needs either, the node's `with` clause has to be widened in the graph. Neither would change the output.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

